republic-overreach.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P3 (S26): "desire more" is taken as wants to outdo others in practising a skill, doing more than its correct standard in P3 C1 A2 and as wants to get more advantage or possessions than others, as Thrasymachus means it where unlike_only is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r3.sense1)
republic-overreach.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {another}; bad = ∅, both = ∅, good = ∅, ignorant = ∅, just = {another}, like_ignorant = ∅, like_wise = ∅, unjust = ∅, unlike_only = {another}, unlike_only_2 = ∅, wise = ∅
republic-overreach.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P4 (S29): "desire more" is taken as wants to outdo everyone in practising a skill, ignoring the craft's standard in P4 C2 A2 and as wants to get more advantage or possessions than everyone where both is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S44) does not follow (republic-overreach.logic.r3.sense2)
republic-overreach.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C (S44): D = {another}; bad = ∅, both = {another}, both_2 = ∅, good = ∅, ignorant = ∅, just = ∅, like_ignorant = ∅, like_wise = ∅, unjust = {another}, unlike_only = ∅, wise = ∅
